1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sultan Johor-Riau ke2; 1528-64.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kesultanan_Johor
2 CONT
2 CONT Sejarah Johor dimulai pada masa pemerintahan Kesultanan Malaka. Sebelumnya daerah Johor merupakan bagian dari Kesultanan Malaka, kemudian Malaka jatuh akibat penaklukan Portugal pada tahun 1511.[1] Berdasarkan Sulalatus Salatin, s
2 CONC etelah wafatnya Sultan Malaka, Mahmud Syah tahun 1528 di Kampar, Sultan Alauddin Syah, salah seorang putra raja Malaka, menjadikan Johor sebagai pusat pemerintahannya dan kemudian dikenal sebagai Kesultanan Johor.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alauddin_Riayat_Shah_II_of_Johor
2 CONT
2 CONT Sultan Alauddin Riayat Shah II was the first Sultan of Johor. He ruled Johor from 1528 to 1564. He founded the Johor Sultanate following the fall of Malacca to the Portuguese in 1511
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sultan_of_Johor
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alauddin_Riayat_Shah_II_of_Johor
2 CONT
2 CONT Sultan Alauddin Riayat Shah II ibni Almarhum Sultan Mahmud Shah (died 1564) was the first Sultan of Johor and ruled from 1528 to 1564. He founded the Johor Sultanate following the fall of Malacca to the Portuguese in 1511. He was 
2 CONC the second son of Mahmud Shah of Malacca. Thus, Johor was a successor state of Malacca and Johor's sultans follow the numbering system of Malacca. Throughout his reign, he faced constant threats from the Portuguese as well as the 
2 CONC emerging Aceh Sultanate.[citation needed]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Sultan Muzaffar Syah. Sultan Pahang ke6; 1530-40.
