2 CONC nduk, educ. privately. Succeeded on the abdication of his father in 1475. Reigned under the regency of his uncle, until superceded by him later that same year. Succeeded on his abdication, 1497. m. at Pahang, after July 1511, … (m
2 CONC . second, ca. 1520, Paduka Sri Sultan 'Abdu'l Jalil ibni al-Marhum Raja Merling, Sultan of Indragiri), daughter of Paduka Sri Sultan Mahmud Shah I ibni al-Marhum Sultan 'Ala' ud-din Ri'ayat Shah Shah, Sultan of Malacca and of Joho
2 CONC r, by his wife, Putri Unang Kening, elder daughter of Paduka Sri Sultan Mansur Shah ibni al-Marhum Sultan Iskandar Shah, Raja of Kelantan. He was k. by his own warriors, ca. 1519, having had issue, two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Raja Puspa Devi. m. Raja Ahmad bin Raja Muhammad, Raja of Trengganu, son of Raja Muhammad ibni al-Marhum Sultan Mansur Shah, Raja of Trengganu, by his wife a female relative of Sultan Mansur - see Malaysia (Kelantan).
