1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sultan Alauddin Riayat Shah III was the 6th Sultan of Johor who reigned from 1597 - 1615. He resided at the new capital of Johor at Batu Sawar, but later moved his administration to Pasir Raja around 1609. Under hi
2 CONC s order in 1612, Bendahara Tun Sri Lanang oversaw the editorial and compilation process of Sejarah Melayu (Malay Annals), the most important Malay literary work of all time.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Between 1613 and 1615, he was captured twice by the Acehnese forces during Aceh-Johor war. In 1615, he was sentenced to death in Acheh and buried in Kota Tinggi, Johor.
2 CONT
