1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sultan Abdul Jalil Shah III merupakan putera kepada Al-Marhum Sultan Alauddin Riayat Shah III [Sultan Johor ke-6, 1597-1616] dengan pasangan baginda Raja Bonda. Sebelum menjadi Sultan, baginda terdahulu dikenali de
2 CONC ngan nama '''Raja Bujang'''. Setelah baginda mangkat, baginda digelar '''Marhum Mangkat''' dan '''Marhum Besar''' di Pahang.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT 1623 - 1677 H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan 'Abdu'l Jalil Shah III ibni al-Marhum Sultan 'Ala' ud-din Ri'ayat Shah III, Khalifat ul-Mukminin Zilu'llah fil'Alam, Sultan of Johor Dar-ul-Izam, Pahang and Lingga. b. 1590, educ. privately. Appo
2 CONC inted as Sultan of Pahang by the Acehnese, August 1615, expelled from Pahang by the Acehnese in 1617, again ruler of Pahang 1623. Succeeded on the death of his uncle, 1623. Entered into treaty relations with the Dutch in 1639 and 
2 CONC assisted them in their capture of Malacca from the Portuguese in 1641. Driven from Johor Lama into exile by the Sultan of Jambi, 1673. m. (first) 1610, his cousin, a daughter of Raja Hassan ibni al-Marhum Sultan Ali Jalla 'Abdu'l 
2 CONC Jalil Shah, Raja of Siak. m. (second) 1612, a daughter of H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Ahmad Shah II ibni al-Marhum Sultan 'Abdu'l-Kadir 'Ala' ud-din Shah, Sultan of Pahang. m. (third) at Patani, 1624 (div.), H.H. Paduka Sri Raja Kuning
2 CONC  binti al-Marhum al-Marhum Sultan 'Abdu'l Ghafur Mohi ud-din Shah [Phra Nang Chao Ying], Raja Perempuan of Patani (b. at Pahang, 1613; m. third, at Patani, 1632 (div.), the Yang di-Pertuan Muda of Johor, and d.s.p. at sea during h
2 CONC er journey to Johore, near Kampung Pancor, Kelantan, 1649, bur. there), only daughter of H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Shah Alam binti al-Marhum Sultan Bahadur Shah, Raja Perempuan of Patani, by her husband, H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan 'Abdu'
2 CONC l Ghafur Muhi ud-din Shah ibni al-Marhum Sultan 'Abdu'l-Kadir 'Ala' ud-din Shah, Sultan of Pahang. He d.s.p. at Kuala Pahang, 22nd November 1677.
