1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1677 - 1685 H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Ibrahim Shah Zilu'llah fil'Alam Khalifat ul-Muminin ibni al-Marhum Yam Tuan Muda Raja Bajau, Sultan of Johor Dar-ul-Izam, Pahang and Lingga, only known son of Raja Bajau ibni al-M
2 CONC arhum Sultan 'Abdu'llah Mu'ayat Shah, Yang di-Pertuan Muda, educ. privately. Succeeded on the death of his cousin, 1677. Established his capital in Riau in order to continue the war with Jambi more effectively. Removed to Johor La
2 CONC ma 1682. m. (first) … m. (second) … m. (third) before 1674, daughter of the Dato Laksamana Paduka Raja. He d. at Riau, 16th February 1685 (poisoned by three of his wives), having had issue:
