1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Pg Anak Sharbanun adalah anak kepada Pg Bendahara Pg Anak Untong. Beliau merupakan cucunda kepada Al-Marhum Sultan 'Abdul Jalilul Jabbar [Sultan Brunei ke-11, 1659-1660]. Semasa hayatnya, Pg Anak Sharbanun ini mend
2 CONC irikan rumahtangga dengan Pg Muda Muhammad 'Alauddin (sebelum menjadi Sultan Muhammad 'Alauddin) kira-kira pada tahun 1710 berputerakan antara lain Pg Muda Amir Bahar dan Pg Muda 'Omar 'Ali Saifuddin. Setelah Pg Babu Sharbanun man
2 CONC gkat, barulah baginda Sultan Muhammad 'Alauddin berkahwin dengan Pg Anak Bulan binti Sultan Husin Kamaluddin.
2 CONT
2 CONT والله أعلمُ
2 CONT ----
2 CONT [https://borneohistory57.blogspot.com/2014/12/sultan-omar-ali-saifuddien-i.html Borneo History]
2 CONT
2 CONT Monday, 29 December 2014
2 CONT Sultan Omar Ali Saifuddien I
2 CONT
2 CONT SOAS I, the 18th Sultan of Brunei was the son of Sultan Muhammad Alauddin and Pengiran Babu Seri Banum. He had 3 wives all of which were the princesses of Sultan Husin Kamaluddin. He had 6 princes (namely Sultan Muhammad Tajuddin 
2 CONC and Sultan Muhammad Kanzul Alam) and a princess.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was believed to be one of the longest serving Sultan (55 years – 1740-1795 cf Sultan Abdul Jalilul Akbar 58 – 1598-1659). He was known for his just rule and wisdom who simply followed the footstep of his father-in-law Sultan Hu
2 CONC sin Kamaluddin. In fact when his father-in-law was still alive, he recieved good knowledge, advice and experience from him during his reigning period.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1775, Sultan of Sulu sent a troop to Brunei headed by Dato Teting to settle the issue of North Borneo (or Sabah) which was a promise made between Sultan Muhyiddin to Sultan of Sulu after the Sulu helped him to a victorious batt
2 CONC le that ended to his favour. The two sides confronted each other that resulted the  surrender of Dato Teting and his troops retreated to Sulu as they found out Brunei’s warriors led by Pengiran Temenggong Ampa ibni Sultan Muhammad
2 CONC  Alauddin (17th) were too superior for them to fight.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the same year according to the textbook Sultan Omar Ali Saifuddien I offered the British Labuan in exchange of protection against Sulu. Thus also explains why Sulu failed to defeat Brunei (the might of British weapons) even tho
2 CONC ugh Sulu and local pirates managed to destroyed the British’s trading post in Balambangan in 1773.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT SOAS I passed away peacefully on 10 July 1795 at Royal Mausoleum. His posthumous name given was Marhum di Makam Besar.
