2 CONT Y.A.M. Raja 'Abdu'l-Hamid ibni al-Marhum Sultan Mansur Shah. He had issue, one son and three daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT i) Y.T.M. Paduka Sri Tuanku Raja Chulan bin Raja 'Abdu'l-Hamid, Raja Muda. Granted the title of Raja Kechil Besar September 1752, prom. to Raja Bendahara April 1766, and appointed as Heir Apparent with the title of Paduka Sri Tuan
2 CONC ku Raja Muda, Wakil us-Sultan, Wazir ul-Azam 1773. A well known historian and author of the "Misa Melayu". m. (first) a Royal wife. m. (second) Che' Mek Anjong, daughter of Dato' 'Usman bin Dato' Haji Besar Daing Selili, Sri Mahar
2 CONC aja Lela, of Kota Lama. He d. at Pulau Juar, 10th February 1787, having had issue, one son and two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Y.M. Raja Kasim bin Raja Chulan (s/o Meh Anjong). m. (div. 1825) Y.A.M. Raja Andak binti al-Marhum Sultan Ahmad ud-din Shah, eldest daughter of H.H. Maulana Paduka Sri Tuanku Sultan Ahmad ud-din Shah ibni al-Marhum Sultan Muha
2 CONC mmad Shah Aminu'llah, Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan of Perak, by his fourth wife, Dato' Nah binti Dato' Jambu, daughter of Dato' Jambu, Kramat Sungkei Durjan. He had issue, one daughter:
