1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1740 - 1760 H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Mahmud 'Abdu'l Jalil Jalal ud-din Muzaffar Shah, Sultan of Siak Sri Indrapura. b. at Lingga, Riau, 1723, second son of H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan 'Abdu'l Jalil Rahmad Shah ibni al-Mar
2 CONC hum Sultan Mahmud Shah, Sultan of Siak, by his second wife, H.H. Tengku Kamariah binti al-Marhum Sultan 'Abdu'l Jalil Ri'ayat Shah, Raja Perempuan, educ. privately. Appointed as Yang di-Pertuan Besar Raja Buang Asmara during his f
2 CONC ather's reign but was forced to flee to Malacca after a dispute with his elder brother, the Raja Muda. Having sort the assistance of the Dutch he conquered Siak with their help, deposed his infirm father, and assumed the reigns of
2 CONC  govt. 1740. m. (first) Dato' Wai, daughter of the Raja Lela Wangsa. m. (second) at Siak, 1731, Daing Metho, Ungku Puan, daughter of Daeng Mattaku, Raja Mas, of Wajo and Selangor, by his wife, Engku Tengah. m. (third) a daughter o
2 CONC f an officer. m. (fourth) …He d. at Mempura Besar, 23rd November 1760 (bur. there), 
