2 CONT 1795 - 1804 and 1804 - 1807 H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Muhammad Taj ud-din ibni al-Marhum Sultan Omar 'Ali Saif ud-din, Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan of Brunei Dar us-Salam, eldest son of H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Omar 'Ali Saif ud-din I ib
2 CONC ni al-Marhum Sultan Muhammad Ala ud-din, Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan of Brunei Dar us-Salam, by his second wife, Paduka Sri Raja Istri Pangiran Anak Nur Alam, educ. privately. Appointed as deputy ruler and invested as Yang di-Pertu
2 CONC an Muda with the personal title of Paduka Sri Sultan Muhammad Taj ud-din ibn Sultan Omar 'Ali Saif ud-din, 1780. Succeeded on the death of his father as Yang di-Pertuan, 10th July 1795. Crowned as Paduka Sri Sultan Muhammad Taj ud
2 CONC -din ibni al-Marhum Sultan Omar 'Ali Saif ud-din. Abdicated in favour of his eldest son, 27th April 1804. Resumed the throne on his death, 10th November 1804. m. (first) H.H. Paduka Sri Raja Istri Pangiran Anak Bulan, daughter of 
2 CONC Y.A.M. Duli Pangiran di-Gadong Sahib ul-Mal ul-Mulk ul-Adli Pangiran Anak 'Abdu'l. m. (second) Y.M. Dayang Asiah, daughter of Mentri Husain. He d. at Brunei Town, 11th February 1807, having had issue:
