1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1450, Sharif ul-Hashim (popularly known as Sayid Abu Bakr), an Arab authority on Islamic religion and law arrived in Buansa, Sulu from Johore, Malacca. He married Princess Paramisuli, the beautiful daughter of R
2 CONC aha Baginda (from Sumatra).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Reference:''' Halili, Maria Christine N. ''Philippine History''. Manila, Philippines. Rex Book Store, Inc., 2004.
