2 CONT ## The Syair Saribas Project http://www.thefreelibrary.com/The+Syair+Saribas+project-a0113055230 An old Malay text has recently come to light which may prove to be one of the most important sources for the history, genealogy and f
2 CONC olkways of the Sarawak Malays. ...  It relates, amongst other things, the arrival at Kuala Saribas of the aristocratic Temenggong Kadir in self-exile from Brunei, to be joined there by the celebrated '''Dato' Godam''' (also known 
2 CONC as Abang Gudam) from Pagar Royong, Minangkabau, in Sumatra who ultimately rescues Kadir's daughter, the beautiful Dayang Chi', from the Sultan of Brunei's harem, marries her and establishes a dynasty. For the most part, however, i
2 CONC t is a closely detailed genealogical and geographical mapping of Malay settlement of the Saribas. At times it has the character of the Old Testament's Book of Genesis, but without the literary quality.
