1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sri Paduka Maharaja Durbaraja II, who became as Sultan Mudzaffar Shah. Paduka Sri Sultan Muzaffar Shah I, Sultan of Kedah. Styled Phra Ong Mahawangsa by the Siamese. Styled Sri Paduka Maharaja Durbar Raja before hi
2 CONC s accession. The first ruler of Kedah to embrace Islam. He d. 27th July 1179
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mudzaffar_Shah_I_of_Kedah
2 CONT
2 CONT Mudzaffar Shah I of Kedah
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT For other people of the same name, see Mudzaffar Shah.
2 CONT Mudzaffar Shah I
2 CONT مظفر شاه ١‎
2 CONT Sultan of Kedah
2 CONT Reign	1136– 27 July 1179
2 CONT Successor	Mu'adzam Shah
2 CONT Died	27 July 1179
2 CONT Issue	Sultan Mu'adzam Shah
2 CONT Tunku Muhammad Shah
2 CONT Tunku Sulaiman Shah
2 CONT House	Mahawangsa
2 CONT Father	Dharmawira of Srivijaya
2 CONT Religion	Sunni Islam
2 CONT
2 CONT Paduka Sri Sultan Mudzaffar Shah I (Jawi: ڤدوك سري سلطان مظفر شاه ١; died 27 July 1179), styled Phra Ong Mahawangsa was a legendary king and was said to be the first Sultan of Kedah, according to the Hikayat Merong Mahawangsa. He 
2 CONC was the last Hindu King of Kedah, styled Sri Paduka Maharaja Durbar Raja before his accession. After his conversion to Islam,[1] he later became the founder of the Kedah Sultanate.
2 CONT
2 CONT See also
2 CONT Merong Mahawangsa
2 CONT
2 CONT References
